1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,700
CHAIRPERSON: Right. Next on the agenda we have traffic and highways. Councillor Thornton.

2
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,386
COUNCILLOR THORNTON: Thank you. Well,

3
00:00:09,386 --> 00:00:14,600
we now have the results of the survey carried out last month about traffic

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,130
and road transport in the town.

5
00:00:16,130 --> 00:00:19,830
People were generally satisfied with the state of the roads.

6
00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:24,386
There were one or two complaints about potholes which will be addressed,

7
00:00:24,386 --> 00:00:32,740
but a significant number of people complained about the increasing number of heavy vehicles using our local roads to avoid traffic elsewhere.

8
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:37,686
We'd expected more complaints by commuters about the reduction in the train service,

9
00:00:37,686 --> 00:00:41,490
but it doesn't seem to have affected people too much.

10
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:47,156
The cycle path that runs alongside the river is very well used by both cyclists

11
00:00:47,156 --> 00:00:50,555
and pedestrians since the surface was improved last year,

12
00:00:50,555 --> 00:00:54,460
but overtaking can be a problem

13
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:58,110
so we're going to add a bit on the side to make it wider.

14
00:00:58,110 --> 00:01:01,260
At some stage, we'd like to extend the path

15
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:04,034
so that it goes all the way through the town,

16
00:01:04,034 --> 00:01:06,840
but that won't be happening in the immediate future.

17
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:15,790
The plans to have a pedestrian crossing next to the Post Office have unfortunately had to be put on hold for the time being.

18
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:18,773
We'd budgeted for this to be done this financial year,

19
00:01:18,773 --> 00:01:22,651
but then there were rumours that the Post Office was going to move,

20
00:01:22,651 --> 00:01:26,230
which would have meant there wasn't really a need for a crossing.

21
00:01:26,230 --> 00:01:29,108
Now they've confirmed that they're staying where they are,

22
00:01:29,108 --> 00:01:34,646
but the Highways Department have told us that it would be dangerous to have a pedestrian crossing

23
00:01:35,028 --> 00:01:38,700
where we'd originally planned it as there's a bend in the road there

24
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:40,820
So that'll need some more thought.

25
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:44,167
On Station Road near the station and level crossing,

26
00:01:44,167 --> 00:01:48,258
drivers can face quite long waits if the level crossing's closed,

27
00:01:48,258 --> 00:01:54,580
and we've now got signs up requesting them not to leave their engines running at that time.

28
00:01:54,580 --> 00:02:01,530
This means pedestrians waiting on the pavement to cross the railway line don't have to breathe in car fumes.

29
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:09,123
We've had some problems with cyclists leaving their bikes chained to the railings outside the ticket office,

30
00:02:09,123 --> 00:02:13,590
but the station has agreed to provide bike racks there.

31
00:02:13,590 --> 00:02:20,280
CHAIRPERSON: So next on the agenda is 'Proposals for improvements to the recreation ground'.

32
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,070
Councillor Thornton again.

33
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:25,806
COUNCILLOR THORNTON: Well, since we managed to extend the recreation ground,

34
00:02:25,806 --> 00:02:32,600
we've spent some time talking to local people about how it could be made a more attractive and useful space.

35
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:35,975
If you have a look at the map up on the screen,

36
00:02:35,975 --> 00:02:38,060
you can see the river up in the north

37
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:41,320
and the Community Hall near the entrance from the road.

38
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:45,360
At present, cars can park between the Community Hall

39
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:47,294
and that line of trees to the east,

40
00:02:47,294 --> 00:02:49,753
but this is quite dangerous for pedestrians

41
00:02:49,753 --> 00:02:56,430
so we're suggesting a new car park on the opposite side of the Community Hall, right next to it.

42
00:02:56,430 --> 00:03:00,170
We also have a new location for the cricket pitch.

43
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:04,818
As we've now purchased additional space to the east of the recreation ground,

44
00:03:04,818 --> 00:03:09,467
beyond the trees, we plan to move it away from its current location,

45
00:03:09,467 --> 00:03:14,830
which is rather near the road, into this new area beyond the line of trees.

46
00:03:14,830 --> 00:03:20,040
This means there's less danger of stray balls hitting cars or pedestrians.

47
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,475
We've got plans for a children's playground

48
00:03:22,475 --> 00:03:26,640
which will be accessible by a footpath from the Community Hall

49
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:28,390
and will be alongside the river.

50
00:03:28,390 --> 00:03:31,820
We'd originally thought of having it close to the road

51
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:34,710
but we think this will be a more attractive location.

52
00:03:34,710 --> 00:03:39,160
The skateboard ramp is very popular with both younger and older children -

53
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:42,497
we had considered moving this up towards the river,

54
00:03:42,497 --> 00:03:48,430
but in the end we decided to have it in the southeast corner near the road.

55
00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:54,420
The pavilion is very well used at present by both football players and cricketers.

56
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:56,415
It will stay where it is now -

57
00:03:56,415 --> 00:03:59,360
to the left of the line of trees and near to the river

58
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:02,400
handy for both the football and cricket pitches.

59
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:07,040
And finally, we'll be getting a new notice board for local information,

60
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:14,000
and that will be directly on people's right as they go from the road into the recreation ground.
